    jl-1a: job log event schema and crash-safe writer

    JOB_LOGS slice jl-1a, as `blit_core::job_log`, library-level:

    - Versioned event schema (format "blit-job-log", version 1): one JSON
      event per line with ts_ms, seq and kind (run-start, phase,
      file-copied, file-deleted, file-failed, stall, diagnostic, summary,
      run-end, log-incomplete); unknown kinds and fields read without error.
    - Logs keyed by run ID + participant + role + attempt, each part
      restricted to a safe, case-free file name.
    - Writer: its own thread fed by a bounded queue (a producer waits rather
      than drop events); appends whole lines to <key>.partial.jsonl, synced
      at phase changes and every 2 s; finish writes run-end, compresses to
      <key>.jsonl.gz through a temp file and one rename, then prunes. A
      sidecar <key>.lock is held throughout, so a reader on Windows can
      still open the active partial.
    - Logging never fails a transfer: on a write failure logging stops, a
      log-incomplete marker is attempted, later events are dropped, and the
      report says the log is incomplete.
    - recover(): finishes partials whose writer is gone, as interrupted
      (keeping a run-end already written); leaves live ones alone.
    - prune(): under a folder lock, keeps the newest `keep` finished logs;
      never touches a partial or a non-log file.

    Adds flate2 (default pure-Rust backend) to blit-core. 21 tests; each of
    16 guard mutations went red. Reading `[jobs] keep` moves to jl-1b, where
    the daemon first writes logs.

