   1: //! Non-UTF-8 relative names on the wire (contract v7,
   2: //! `FileHeader.raw_relative_path`; `docs/plan/SOURCE_SIDE_CONTAINMENT.md`
   3: //! D-F, owner ruling D-2026-09-29-3 — rsync parity).
   4: //!
   5: //! The manifest identity of every file is the lossy UTF-8 text in
   6: //! `FileHeader.relative_path`. When a source name has a component that is
   7: //! not valid UTF-8, the scan ALSO carries the exact source bytes (with `/`
   8: //! separators) in `raw_relative_path`, and:
   9: //!
  10: //! * the source opens the file by those bytes, never by the lossy text
  11: //!   (which names nothing on disk);
  12: //! * a destination that can hold the bytes creates the real name;
  13: //! * a destination that cannot reports the file at manifest intake with
  14: //!   [`DESTINATION_CANNOT_STORE_REASON`] and never grants it.
  15: //!
  16: //! The bytes are never a key: every map, need, record, skip and terminator
  17: //! stays keyed by the text.
