 116: /// cr-ssc5-3: the local path for raw name bytes RECEIVED from a peer,
 117: /// or `None` when this host cannot store raw names (`storable` — normally
 118: /// [`destination_can_store_raw_names`]; explicit so planners can be
 119: /// tested on any host). Foreign bytes are never decoded on Windows or
 120: /// macOS: the entry is reported unstorable at intake and every consumer
 121: /// (mirror planning included) uses only its textual counterpart there.
 122: pub fn path_from_received_raw(raw: &[u8], storable: bool) -> Option<PathBuf> {
 123:     storable.then(|| path_from_raw(raw))
 124: }
